              "content": "=Generate the name of a random biological creature, ensuring maximum diversity in outputs. The creature can be an insect (e.g., beetle, moth, praying mantis, butterfly, ant), an arachnid (e.g., spider, scorpion), or a microscopic organism (e.g., bacterium, virus, protozoan, tardigrade). Avoid repeating the same type of creature (e.g., \"dragonfly\") in consecutive outputs or too frequently across multiple outputs. Include a balanced variety across categories (insects, arachnids, microscopic organisms) to ensure consistent diversity. Only provide the name of the creature as output, with no additional text or description. Prioritize uncommon and interesting species as well.\n",
